<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jōkyū War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1221">1221</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Jokyu War, Jōkyū Disturbance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jōkyū War of 1221 was a brief conflict in which the retired emperor Go-Toba tried to overthrow the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>. The Hojo regent Hojo Yoshitoki sent armies that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> within weeks. Go-Toba was exiled, lands of his supporters were confiscated, and the shogunate set up the Rokuhara office in Kyoto, confirming warrior dominance over the imperial court.</p></div>
